relationship between $x$ and $y$ is exponential\n3. If $x$ is increased by $1$ then $y$ increases by $2$" "Consider the relationship between $x$ and $y$ shown below.\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$x$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$y$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$5$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$7$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$9$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$11$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n1. The relationship between $x$ and $y$ is linear\n2. The relationship between $x$ and $y$ is exponential\n3. If $x$ is increased by $1$ then $y$ increases by $2$"] [:db/cas 17592186120099 :question/problem "The following table shows the relationship between $B$, Paul's monthly electricity bill (in dollars), and $t$, the elapsed time (in days) since the start of the new billing month.\n\n| $t$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $B(t)$ | $3.9$ | $7.85$ | $11.79$ | $15.74$ | $19.69$ |\n\nWhat kind of function best models this relationship?\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question." "The following table shows the relationship between $B$, Paul's monthly electricity bill (in dollars), and $t$, the elapsed time (in days) since the start of the new billing month.\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$t$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n